  m_Name: Lore-en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  language: 0
  title: 
  text: 'Between 1994 and 1996, Harrow Creek lived in fear. The "Harrow Creek Butcher" claimed six victims and left the same signature on every one: a kitchen knife from the victim''s own home.


    Ethan Myers, a crime reporter for the Harrow Creek Ledger, covered the case from the first body to the last, alongside photographer Clara Reyes.


    In 1996, the killings stopped. Clara vanished that same week. Police closed the case and declared their main suspect dead. No one was ever arrested.'
  displayDuration: 30
  isSkippable: 1
